The wire format's users, not just the wire format.

M160's patch 0041 gated the MOJOM for net::AddressTrackerLinux's output on
has_linux_kernel - rtnetlink is a system call family rather than a platform
family - and said in its own message that a feature is only off when the last
site turning it on is. It found two sites. There were seven.

The five that were left are the C++ that USES the generated types:
network::NetworkChangeManager implements mojom::NetworkInterfaceChangeListener
and holds a receiver for it, NetworkService reads
params->initial_address_map, and content/browser's two network service files
include net/base/address_tracker_linux.h, whose first line is
#include <linux/rtnetlink.h>.

The seventh is in //net itself and is the sharpest of them:
NetworkChangeNotifierPassive declares GetAddressMapOwnerInternal() as an
override under plain IS_LINUX, while M150 had already widened the base
class's declaration to (IS_LINUX || IS_CHROMEOS) && HAS_LINUX_KERNEL. A
derived class overriding a method that is not there is a compile error in a
file nothing about this port had touched.

18 of the 86.

